    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "RMKzs",
      "x": 6300,
      "y": -120,
      "name": "Failover flow note",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Storm-time failover flow. Today the live UI is a stub: Tools → Failover, then Preview plan, then Run failover. This board is the designed path — pick apps, review dumps, repoint connection strings, run, paste haproxy, restore home. Step 05 exists because a copied Secret still holds the home address. The rule is deliberately blunt: one Postgres comes up on DigitalOcean and everything points straight at it, so poolers, tailnet load balancers and NodePorts are rewritten rather than recreated."
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "h7Yohw",
      "x": 6300,
