    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "M8fRJR",
      "x": 6300,
      "y": 2560,
      "name": "Destination wizard note",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Configuring a destination, before any of the Failover screens can do anything. Five steps in a dialog over Settings, because picking a provider, proving the credentials work, sizing the copy and describing the edge are four different decisions and a flat form hides that. Step 1 has one real option today and is built so AWS is another card, not a rewrite. Step 2 validates against the DigitalOcean API before saving rather than failing later during a storm. Step 4 is optional on purpose: there is no default edge, because a snippet naming someone else's proxy is worse than none."
    },
